From: TNG Technical Manual compatibility investigation
Subject: [PATCH] DIRECTOR: Hide Trek Tech leading article marker

Some Trek Tech article files begin with a legacy 0xA5 formatting marker.
The Windows Trek font renders that marker as a stray percent sign. Strip it
at read time only when it is the first byte, preserving original disc data.
---
 engines/director/lingo/xlibs/f/fileio.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/f/fileio.cpp b/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/f/fileio.cpp
index 76a2cccf..c7bbb7cf 100644
--- a/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/f/fileio.cpp
+++ b/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/f/fileio.cpp
@@ -555,6 +555,13 @@ void FileIO::m_readFile(int nargs) {
 		ch = me->_inStream->readByte();
 	}
 
+	// Several Trek Tech article files begin with a legacy 0xA5 formatting
+	// marker. The bundled Windows font renders it as a stray percent sign.
+	// Strip only a leading marker for this title, leaving the original disc
+	// data untouched and preserving any byte used within actual text.
+	if (Common::String(g_director->getGameId()).equals("trektech") && !res.empty() && (byte)res[0] == 0xA5)
+		res.deleteChar(0);
+
 	g_lingo->push(res);
 }
 
